!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
! METHYL VINYL KETONE c2h3coch3
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

! MethylVinyl Ketone unimolecular decomposition reactions
! Rate constants calculated by solving the ME/RRKM equations with the MESMER software
! The association ILT approach has been adopted. The rate constants of the association steps are provided as well as the 
! G3//M06-2X/aug-cc-pVDZ ZPE corrected 0K energies. The vibrations frequencies and the torsional PES
! of each single species (reactant and products) were calculated at the M06-2X/aug-cc-pVDZ level.
! The energy tranfer model adopted is <Edown> = 200 * (T/300)^0.85 1/cm
! The association rate constants adopted are as follow:
! (1) c2h3co + ch3 = c2h3coch3:    1.632E+14 * T^-0.377 * exp(37.6/T)
!    the rate constant calculated by Saxena et al. (Proceedings of the Combustion Institute (2009),
!    Vol. 32, pp. 123–130) for the reaction ch3co+ch3 has been adopted as it
! (2) c2h3 + ch2co = c2h3coch3:    2.120E+14 * T^-0.401 * exp(95.3/T)
!    the rate constant calculated by Saxena has been corrected to account for the change between methyl and vinyl
!    k(c2h3+ch2co) = k(ch3+ch3co) * k(ch3+c2h5) / k (ch3+ch3)
!    the rate constants for methyl-methyl and methyl-ethyl recombination were adopted from Klippenstein et al.
!    (Physical Chemistry Chemical Physics (2006), Vol. 8, pp. 1133–1141)
! (3) h + c2h3coch2 = c2h5coch3:  5.833E+13 * T^0.176 * exp(63/T)
!    the rate constant is assumed to be the same as the one for the reaction h + c3h5-a = c3h6
!    Harding et al., Journal of Physical Chemistry A (2007) Vol. 111, pp. 3789-3801

c2h3coch3(+m)<=>ch3co+c2h3(+m)         2.576E+22    -1.732   92775.2
